ex website located at https://www.Cemex.com and any subsite of such website (the “Website”). For purposes of this Privacy Statement, “Personal Information” is data specifically about you, which you typically provide on a voluntary basis. Aggregate or combined information includes data that is related to you but studied as a group and does not identify you specifically. You cannot “opt-out” from having aggregate information collected except as otherwise specified in this Privacy Statement. Cemex, S.A.B. de C.V. (“Cemex SAB”), a Mexican publicly traded stock corporation with variable capital that has a registered address at Avenida Ricardo Margain Zozaya #325, Colonia Valle del Campestre, San Pedro Garza Garcia, Nuevo Leon, 66265, Mexico, is the controller of your Personal Information. This means that it determines the purpose for which, and the means by which, your Personal Information is used and it is responsible for handling your information in accordance with Mexican and European Union (“EU”) law, as well as any other applicable data protection law. For the purpose of this Privacy Statement, Cemex Operaciones México, S.A. de C.V. (“Cemex Operaciones México”), a Mexican wholly-owned subsidiary of Cemex SAB that has a registered address at Avenida Ricardo Margain Zozaya #325, Colonia Valle del Campestre, San Pedro Garza Garcia, Nuevo Leon, 66265, Mexico, is also a joint controller in respect of your Personal Information. Since Cemex Operaciones México provides back office services to Cemex SAB in relation to the Website, in certain circumstances, they will jointly decide how your Personal Information is held and used; nevertheless, Cemex SAB will be responsible for answering any data subject request as set forth in this Privacy Statement. This Privacy Statement is issued by Cemex SAB on behalf of Cemex Operaciones México. .component-paragraph img { max-width: 100%; } II. Your Rights in Relation to Your Personal Information .fragment-heading-text-colored a { color: inherit; } You may review, correct and update certain Personal Information (such as your name and contact information) by contacting us using the information in the “Contact Us” section below. Under certain circumstances, you can also: Request access to your Personal Information. You can request to receive a copy of the Personal Information we hold about you and verify that we are lawfully processing it. Request correction of your Personal Information. You can ask us to correct any incomplete or inaccurate information we hold about you. We encourage you to provide us with accurate Personal Information and to let us know if your Personal Information changes. We will not assume any liability in respect of incorrect Personal Information you provide to us. Request erasure of your Personal Information. You can request to delete or remove Personal Information where there is no good reason for us to continue using or storing it. You also have the right to ask us to delete or remove your Personal Information where you have exercised your right to object to us using it, as described below. Object to our use of your Personal Information where we are relying on our legitimate interest (or those of a third party) to do so and there is something about your particular situation which makes you want to object to us using it on this ground. Request restriction of the use of your Personal Information. You can ask us to suspend the use of your Personal Information, for example, if you want us to determine its accuracy. Request the transfer of your Personal Information in an accessible format to you or another organization. Withdraw your consent to the use of your Personal Information. Where you have consented to our use of your Personal Information for a specific purpose, you have the right to withdraw your consent for that specific use at any time. Once you have withdrawn your consent, we will no longer process your Personal Information for the purpose(s) you originally consented to, unless we are required to keep it to comply with the applicable law. Please note that the withdrawal of your consent will not affect the lawfulness of our use of your Personal Information before you withdraw your consent. In order to exercise any of the rights mentioned above, you should send us a request, through any of the means mentioned in the “Contact Us” section, that includes the following: your name, address, phone number and e-mail address (our response to your request will be sent to this e-mail address); when applicable, the name of your legal representative including a copy of the document evidencing the validity of the such legal representation; a copy of any official ID and, when applicable, the ID of your legal representative; an indication of the right(s) mentioned above you wish to exercise as well as a clear and precise description of the Personal Information upon which such rights will be exercised, including any changes to be made to your Personal Information if applicable, and any other element or document which relates to your request or which may help us in locating your Personal Information. Exercising one of your rights mentioned above is not a prerequisite for and does not preclude you from exercising any other right. In case the information provided is erroneous or insufficient, or the required documentation in order to confirm your identity are not attached, within 5 business days following the receipt of your request, we may solicit that you provide us the necessary elements or documents to process your request. You will have 10 business days from the date in which you receive our solicitation in order to fulfill it. If you do not respond in the aforementioned period, your request will be considered as not submitted. Cemex will inform you of the resolution within 20 business days from the date in which we received your request, so that, if resolved favorably, it is executed within 15 business days from the date in which we inform you of the resolution. For more information on the process or requirements to exercise any of the abovementioned rights, as well as for any questions you may have in relation to the processing of your Personal Information, please contact us by using the information in the “Contact Us” section below. .component-paragraph img { max-width: 100%; } III. Collected Information .fragment-heading-text-colored a { color: inherit; } You may review, correct and update certain Personal Information (such as your name and contact information) by contacting us using the information in the “Contact Us” section below. Under certain circumstances, you can also: Request access to your Personal Information. You can request to receive a copy of the Personal Information we hold about you and verify that we are lawfully processing it. Request correction of your Personal Information. You can ask us to correct any incomplete or inaccurate information we hold about you. We encourage you to provide us with accurate Personal Information and to let us know if your Personal Information changes. We will not assume any liability in respect of incorrect Personal Information you provide to us. Request erasure of your Personal Information. You can request to delete or remove Personal Information where there is no good reason for us to continue using or storing it. You also have the right to ask us to delete or remove your Personal Information where you have exercised your right to object to us using it, as described below. Object to our use of your Personal Information where we are relying on our legitimate interest (or those of a third party) to do so and there is something about your particular situation which makes you want to object to us using it on this ground. Request restriction of the use of your Personal Information. You can ask us to suspend the use of your Personal Information, for example, if you want us to determine its accuracy. Request the transfer of your Personal Information in an access