 img { max-width: 100%; } IV. Use and Sharing of Personal Information .fragment-heading-text-colored a { color: inherit; } 1. Use of Personal Information Cemex may use your Personal Information to communicate with you in relation to your questions, comments or requests made through the Website, to send you any information including sending you automated alerts containing financial information as requested by you through the Website, to process your pre-registration to Cemex Go when applicable, as well as for other purposes and activities as set forth in the table below. Additionally, Cemex may use your Personal Information collected through cookies or similar technologies as mentioned above, for performance, analysis and marketing purposes. You are not obligated to provide us with any Personal Information but please note that this may result in us being unable to provide you with the requested services, prevent us from effectively responding to your comments or questions made through the Website or prevent the Website from remembering any preferences you have set in relation to its performance. We rely on a number of legal bases to process the Personal Information of users in the European Economic Area (“EEA”) as described in the table below. We have also identified what our legitimate interests are where appropriate. .component-paragraph img { max-width: 100%; } table { width: 100%; background-color: #f0f5ff; border-collapse: collapse; border-width: 2px; border-color: #ffffff; border-style: solid; color: #272833; } table, td, th { border-width: 2px; border-color: #ffffff; border-style: solid; padding: 2px; } table thead { background-color: #0003B1; color: white; } @media(max-width:767px){ table{ overflow:scroll; } } Purpose / Activity Lawful basis for processing including basis of legitimate interest To register you as a new customer, including pre-registration in Cemex Go, or a new supplier Performance of a contract with you To manage our relationship with you which may include: (a) Answering any questions or comments you make through the Website (b) Notifying you about changes to our terms or privacy statement (c) Asking you to leave a review or take a survey (a) Performance of a contract with you (b) Necessary to comply with a legal obligation (c) Necessary for our legitimate interests (to keep our records updated and to study how customers use our products/services to develop them and grow our business) To enable you to partake in a prize draw or competition (a) Performance of a contract with you (b) Necessary for our legitimate interests (to study how customers use our products/services, to develop them and grow our business) To administer and protect our business and this website (including troubleshooting, data analysis, testing, system maintenance, support, reporting and hosting of data) (a) Necessary for our legitimate interests (for running our business, provision of administration and IT services, network security, to prevent fraud and in the context of a business reorganisation or group restructuring exercise) (b) Necessary to comply with a legal obligation To deliver relevant website content and advertisements to you and measure or understand the effectiveness of the advertising we serve to you Necessary for our legitimate interests (to study how customers use our products/services, to develop them, to grow our business and to inform our marketing strategy) To use data analytics to improve our website, products/services, marketing, customer relationships and experiences Necessary for our legitimate interests (to define types of customers for our products and services, to keep our website updated and relevant, to develop our business and to inform our marketing strategy) To make suggestions and recommendations to you about goods or services that may be of interest to you Necessary for our legitimate interests (to develop our products/services and grow our business) To send you any alert, newsletter or other marketing communications Data subject consent .component-html img { max-width: 100%; } Note that we may process your personal data for more than one lawful ground depending on the specific purpose for which we are using your data. Please contact us using the \"Contact Us\" information below if you need details about the specific legal ground we are relying on to process your personal data where more than one ground has been set out in the table above. Additionally, if you are an EEA user and wish to learn more about our legitimate interests in using the Personal Information and how we have balanced our interests against your fundamental rights and interests, please contact us using the \"Contact Us\" information below. If you provide Personal Information to Cemex, you agree to the use, collection and disclosure of the Personal Information by Cemex for the purposes described in this Privacy Statement. 2. Sharing of Personal Information In order to provide the services related to the Website, Cemex may share certain Personal Information with third parties acting on our behalf, including: .component-paragraph img { max-width: 100%; } table { width: 100%; background-color: #f0f5ff; border-collapse: collapse; border-width: 2px; border-color: #ffffff; border-style: solid; color: #272833; } table, td, th { border-width: 2px; border-color: #ffffff; border-style: solid; padding: 2px; } table thead { background-color: #0003B1; color: white; } Third Party Purpose Ilinium Provider of the services for developing the Website and implementing any changes. .component-html img { max-width: 100%; } Cemex may disclose your information (including your Personal Information), as necessary, to regulators, courts, legal advisers and law enforcement authorities: (1) if we determine a policy violation has occurred; (2) if we believe such disclosure is necessary to identify, contact or bring legal action regarding injury or interference with the rights and property of Cemex, including to enforce Cemex’s rights against unauthorized access or attempted unauthorized access to Cemex's information technology assets or against other inappropriate use of the Website; (3) to comply with laws, regulations, court orders and subpoenas or similar requests for information by authorities, or as otherwise required by law; (4) to protect your safety and the safety of others; and (5) to assist us in fraud prevention or investigation. We have a legitimate interest in sharing the Personal Information of EU users for purposes (1) and (2). .component-paragraph img { max-width: 100%; } V. Opting-out of Our Mailing List .fragment-heading-text-colored a { color: inherit; } Cemex will only send you marketing or promotional communications or communications about other topics if you have provided your consent to receive these types of communications. To contact you, Cemex may use the information you provide to us, including email, address, fax or phone. You may, at any time, inform us that you no longer want Cemex to contact you for marketing purposes by sending your request to us using the contact information in the “Contact Us” section below. You may also opt-out of promotional email communications by clicking on a link provided in the promotional email message. After opting-out, you will no longer receive marketing or promotional communications from us. .component-paragraph img { max-width: 100%; } VI. Tracking .fragment-heading-text-colored a { color: inherit; } Certain web browsers may provide a do-not-track (“DNT”) option. You may be able to ask your browser to inform websites that you do not wish your activities to be tracked, either with cookies or other persistent identifiers, commonly called “DNT signals.” The Website currently does not respond to DNT signals. However, we do not track your online activities over time across different websites. .component-paragraph img { max-width: 100%; } VII. Safeguarding Your Information .fragment-heading-text-colored a { color: inherit; } Cemex is committed to maintaining the security of the data you provide us. However, please note that there is always some risk in transmitting information over the Internet. When you use the Website, your communications may be intercepted by others. For this reason, Cemex cannot guarantee the security and privacy of transmissions via the Internet, and we will not be liable for any lack of security relating to the use of the Website by you. You agree that you will not hold Cemex liable for any damages resulting from any loss of privacy or security occurring in connection with any communications over such networks. .component-paragraph img { max-width: 100%; } VII. Transfers of Personal Information Outside of The EEA .fragment-heading-text-colored a { color: inherit; } Cemex is a worldwide corporate group. By using our Website, you authorize us to transfer and store your information outside of your home country, including in the EEA, for the purposes described in this Privacy Statement. Where we transfer Personal Information from the EEA to a country that does not provide an adequate level of protection, we will only do so under appropriate safeguards put in place to protect your information, such as standard contractual clauses. Outside of the EEA, Personal Information may be transferred mainly to Mexico and the United States, although certain contact forms within the Website may give you the option to transmit your Personal Information to other regions. If you would like more information about these safeguards, please contact us using the information in the \"Contact Us\" section below. .component-paragraph img { max-width: 100%; } IX. Automated Decision-making .fragment-heading-text-colored a { color: inherit; } We do not envisage that any decisions will be taken about you using automated means. .component-paragraph img { max-width: 100%; } X. How Long We Keep Your Personal Information For .fragment-heading-text-colored a { color: inherit; } We will only retain your Personal Information for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes we collected it for, including for the purposes of satisfying any legal, accounting, or reporting requirements. To determine the appropriate retention period for your Personal Information, we consider the amount, nature, and sensitivity of the Personal Information, the potential risk of harm from unauthorized use or disclosure of your Personal Information, the purposes for which we process your Personal Information and whether we can achieve those purposes through other means, and the applicable requirements. When we no longer need to use your Personal Information as mentioned above and there is no need for us to keep it to comply with our legal or regulatory obligations, we will either remove it from our systems or depersonalize it so that we cannot identify you. For further information on retention periods please contact us by using the information in the “Contact Us” section below. .component-paragraph img { max-width: 100%; } XI. Exclusions .fragment-heading-text-colored a { color: inherit; } The Website may contain links external websites, such as the job application website, that may be subject to a different privacy statement. We recommend that you carefully review the privacy statement of each website you visit. Cemex is not responsible for the content or privacy practices of websites owned by other companies. This Privacy Statement addresses Cemex's procedures for handling the Personal Information of users who have reached the age of majority. We do not seek to, nor do we knowingly collect, information from minors. If a minor has provided us with Personal Information, a parent or guardian of that minor may contact us to have the information deleted from our records. To do so, contact Cemex through the information provided below in the “Contact Us” section. .component-paragraph img { max-width: 100%; } XII. Contact Us .fragment-heading-text-colored a { color: inherit; } Cemex has a Chief Privacy Officer located in Mexico, as well as Data Protection Officers in European countries where we have operations. You may contact Cemex's data privacy office at any time if you have questions, general concerns about the processing of your personal information, or any data protection issue, by sending an e-mail to dataprivacy@cemex.com . Additionally, for the benefit of EEA data subjects and pursuant to article 27 of the General Data Protection Regulation, we have appointed Cemex España, S.A. (“Cemex España”), a Spanish corporation that has a registered address at Avenida de Burgos, 19, 28036 Madrid, Spain, as our representative in the EU. If you are an EEA data subject, you may address Cemex España as to any issues relating to the processing of your Personal Information under this Privacy Statement in addition to or instead of the controllers mentioned above which are located in Mexico. You can contact Cemex España by sending an e-mail to dataprivacyeurope@cemex.com . If you are a Mexican user and you consider that we have infringed upon your personal data protection rights, you have the right to make a complaint to the Personal Data Transparency, Access and Protection National Institute (Instituto Nacional de Transparencia, Acceso a la Información y Protección de Datos Personales). For more information, please visit www.inai.org.mx . If you are an EEA user and you feel that we have not answered your concerns appropriately you have the right to make a complaint to your local data protection authority. Contact details for EU data protection authorities can be found here . If you are located elsewhere and consider we have infringed upon your personal data protection rights, please contact your local data protection authority for more information on how to exercise your right to file a complaint. In any case, we would appreciate the chance to deal with your concerns before you approach the corresponding data protection authority, so please contact us in the first instance. .component-paragraph img { max-width: 100%; } XIII. Updates to Privacy Statement .fragment-heading-text-colored a { color: inherit; } From time to time, we may update this Privacy Statement. If we do, we will note near the top of this page the date that any changes are made or when they become effective. If the changes being made are material, we may alert you to the changes in a more prominent way. Your inaction or continued use of the Website, after any such notices, will tell us that you agree to these changes. .component-paragraph img { max-width: 100%; } About Cemex Cemex is a multinational construction materials company focused on building a better future for communities worldwide. The company produces and markets cement, ready-mix concrete, aggregates, and related construction materials such as admixtures and mortars, enabling construction projects across its markets. Through customer-centric solutions, operational excellence, and continuous innovation, Cemex delivers high-performance materials that meet the industry's evolving needs. With a workforce of around 40,000 people worldwide, Cemex provides reliable, sustainable, and high-quality products and services, partnering with its customers to deliver solutions that create long-term value. About Us .fragment_2201 button { background: none; color: inherit; border: none; padding: 0; font: inherit; cursor: pointer; outline: inherit; } .fragment_2201 .text-with-download-link #link-wrapper{ margin-left:-10px; } .fragment_2201 .text-with-download-link .material-symbols-outlined::after { content: \"arrow_forward\"; } .fragment_2201 .text-with-download-link { display: inline-flex; font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; line-height: normal; letter-spacing: normal; column-gap: 10px; } .fragment_2201 .link-text { font-weight: 700; flex-grow: 0; } .fragment_2201 .link-text, .fragment_2201 .link-text:hover { text-decoration: none; } .fragment_2201 .arrow-text-style a, .fr